{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecay","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecay","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnot","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.FractionRing","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.GCD.Basic"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.jet_levels_sigma4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.jet_levels_sigma4","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L329-L336","doc":"The jet bundle over Σ₄ has exactly 3 non-zero levels (0, 1, 2).\nDegree 1: 4 knots. Degree 2: 2 knots. Degree ≥ 3: none. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.no_degree3_on_sigma4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.no_degree3_on_sigma4","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L323-L327","doc":"No degree-3 torus knot embeds on Σ₄.\n`τ(2, 3³) = τ(2, 27)` needs genus `(1)(26)/2 = 13 > 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.interaction_completeness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.interaction_completeness","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L259-L319","doc":"**Theorem (interaction completeness).**\nThe 6 embeddable torus knots on Σ₄ exhaust the harmonic 1-forms\non the fiber.  Every transfer matrix (= force operator) is a\ncomposition of these 6.  No 7th interaction exists.\n\nProof: a 7th embeddable torus knot τ(r,s) with (r-1)(s-1)/2 ≤ 4\nand gcd(r,s) = 1 does not exist (exhaustive enumeration).\nThe next candidate τ(2,11) requires genus 5 > 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.spectralDecompositionQValue_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.spectralDecompositionQValue_def","kind":"instance","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L236-L241","doc":"Default instance when `qValue` is *defined* as the product\n`qBare * knotProd` (rather than asserted to equal it). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralDecompositionQValue.factorisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralDecompositionQValue.factorisation","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L234-L234","doc":"`qValue = qBare · knotProd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralDecompositionQValue.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralDecompositionQValue.mk","kind":"ctor","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L229-L229","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SpectralDecompositionQValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SpectralDecompositionQValue","kind":"class","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L200-L234","doc":"**Spectral decomposition Q-value — typeclass.**\n\nFor β⁻ decay on Σ_g, the Q_q-value decomposes as:\n\n`Q_q = Q_bare × ∏_{τ(r,s) ∈ E_g} F(τ(r,s), N)`\n\nwhere:\n- `Q_bare = |log_q(P_dau/P_par)| · ℏ_q · m_e/3`\n- `F(τ, N)` is the knot operator\n- The product collapses to a single active term\n- The decomposition is exact (completeness of torus knot basis)\n\n**Proof structure:**\n1. Completeness: Rosso–Jones + self-duality → complete basis\n2. Inductive chain: zero Hecke steps, Gröbner normal form\n3. Shell cancellation: parent/daughter share inner chains\n4. Pauli projection: full shell → alternating irrep\n5. Tower termination: degree ≥ 3 needs genus > 4\n\nPer-`op` witness that the Q-value of a β-decay operator\nequals `Q_bare · ∏ (knot-operator product)`. Full proof requires:\n(1) Rosso–Jones completeness (external),\n(2) inductive chain construction (`TransferMatrix.lean`),\n(3) shell cancellation,\n(4) Pauli projection (Young symmetrizer),\n(5) tower termination (embeddability bound).\nUntil those land, the equality is per-instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.knotOperator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.knotOperator","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L174-L196","doc":"The knot operator `F(τ, N)` for torus knot `τ` at neutron\nnumber `N` on a genus-`g` surface.\n\nThis is defined over `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]` via the Markov trace of\nthe torus knot element composed with the beta decay operator\nin `H₃(q)`.\n\nThe operator is:\n- `1` if `τ` is not embeddable (null: zero action)\n- `1` if `τ`'s shell is not active (cancels in parent/daughter)\n- `markovTrace_knot_beta τ` if active shell, partially filled\n  (the `(t+t⁻¹)` normalisation is absorbed into `Q_bare`)\n- `pauliProjectedKnotOp τ` if active shell, fully filled\n  (Pauli exclusion projects to sign representation) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pauliProjectedKnotOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pauliProjectedKnotOp","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L155-L170","doc":"The Pauli-projected knot operator for fully filled shells.\n\nFor a full shell, the antisymmetrizer `e_{(1^r)}` projects onto\nthe sign representation of `S_r`.  The Pauli-projected knot\noperator reduces to the determinant sign:\n\n`det(T_pp)^{(r-1)·s}` where `det(T_pp) = −(𝔴⁺)²·HA = −HA`\n(since `𝔴⁺_pp = 1`).\n\nThe determinant of a single crossing matrix `T(c,d)` is:\n`det = (c·HA + d)·d − c² = c·HA·d + d² − c²`.\nFor pp: `c=1, d=0`, so `det = 0 − 1 = −1`.\n\nThus the Pauli factor is `(-1)^{(r-1)·s}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.markovTrace_knot_beta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.markovTrace_knot_beta","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L150-L153","doc":"Cleared Markov trace of `τ · T_{β-decay}`:\n`(t + t⁻¹) · tr_M(τ · T_{β-decay})` in `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotMatrix","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L138-L148","doc":"The transfer matrix for a torus knot `τ(r,s)`.\n\nThe torus knot braid word is `(σ₁σ₂…σ_{r-1})^s`, which gives\na product of `r-1` crossing matrices repeated `s` times.\n\nFor the knot operator, we compute the product of crossing matrices\nalong the knot's braid representative.  We define this as the\n`s`-th power of the single-period transfer matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shellFilled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shellFilled","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L132-L134","doc":"Whether a shell is fully filled: `N ≥ cap(shell)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shellActive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shellActive","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L127-L130","doc":"Whether a shell is active for a given neutron number.\nShell `k` is active if `prevCap(k) < N ≤ cap(k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.prevShellCapacity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.prevShellCapacity","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L121-L125","doc":"Previous shell capacity (lower bound for the active range). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shellCapacity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shellCapacity","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L109-L119","doc":"Cumulative shell capacities from the magic numbers.\nShell `k` is filled when `N ≥ shellCapacity k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.markovTrace_beta_decay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.markovTrace_beta_decay","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L102-L105","doc":"Cleared Markov trace of the beta decay operator:\n`(t + t⁻¹) · tr_M(T_{β-decay})` in `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.T_beta_decay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.T_beta_decay","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L89-L100","doc":"The beta decay transfer matrix `T_{β-decay} = σ₀ · σ₁⁻¹` in H₃(q).\n\nUsing the Hecke relation `σ⁻¹ = σ − (q − q⁻¹)`,\nwe have `T_{β-decay} = σ₀σ₁ − (q − q⁻¹)σ₀`.\n\nAs a 2×2 matrix: the decay changes one nn crossing to a pn\ncrossing at the converting vertex.  The net effect on the\ntransfer matrix chain is to replace `T_nn` by `T_pn` at the\nconverting site.  In the doubled integral form, this is\n`two_T_pn` (the pn crossing matrix). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.skeinRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.skeinRatio","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L53-L71","doc":"The Skein polynomial ratio `P_dau / P_par` in the fraction field.\n\nSince we work with cleared Skein polynomials (multiplied by\npowers of `t + t⁻¹`), the ratio is an element of the fraction\nfield of `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`.  For the Q-value, we need `log_q` of\nthis ratio, which counts exceptional divisor levels.\n\nWe embed both polynomials into `FractionRing R_t` (the field of\nfractions of the integral domain `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`) and perform\ndivision there.  The `algebraMap` coercion is the canonical\nembedding `R_t →+* FractionRing R_t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp.is_beta_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp.is_beta_minus","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L45-L45","doc":"The daughter differs by exactly one nucleon: n → p. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp.daughter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp.daughter","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L43-L43","doc":"Daughter nuclear configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp.parent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp.parent","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Parent nuclear configuration. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp.mk","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BetaDecayOp","kind":"structure","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BetaDecay.lean#L27-L49","doc":"The beta decay operator `T_{β-decay}(q) = σ₀ · σ₁⁻¹` in `H₃(q)`.\n\nThis is the universal `±1` transition operator: it changes one\nneutron crossing to a proton crossing (or vice versa) at the\nconverting vertex.\n\nIn the Gröbner–Shirshov framework, `σ₁⁻¹ = σ₁ − (q − q⁻¹)`,\nso `T_{β-decay} = σ₀σ₁ − (q − q⁻¹)σ₀`.\n\nAs a 2×2 matrix, the decay changes the crossing coefficients\nat the converting generator from `(𝔴⁺_nn, 𝔴⁰_nn)` to\n`(𝔴⁺_pn, 𝔴⁰_pn)` (or vice versa). ","signatureChunk":0}]}